cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cited for the 'as short as practical' principle on certificate
  lifetimes and for the risk-based, no-fixed-year framing that RFD 2145 adopts."
title: "In-house PKI: keep certificate lifetimes as short as practical"
type: standard
authors:
  - name: "National Cyber Security Centre (UK)"
url: "https://www.ncsc.gov.uk/collection/in-house-public-key-infrastructure/pki-principles/keep-certificate-lifetimes-as-short-as-practical"
license: "OGL v3.0"
notes: "'Certificates should have lifetimes that are as short as practical,
  while balancing the operational overhead of renewal.' Directional rather
  than prescriptive. RFD 2145 reads this as 'the cadence you can actually
  hold to' — 5 years for the root ceremony, 1 year for the intermediate
  rotation, <=45 days for automated leaf rotation."
